# Decision Canvas

Spec: DecisionCanvas
Purpose:
  Standard template for every engineering decision. Ensures all
  required inputs are present before a decision is recorded.

Template:
  QUESTION:
    <exact question being answered>

  CONTEXT:
    @context.CTX<id>
    <project state, constraints, history>

  FACTS:
    - @fact.F<id>: <statement>
    - @fact.F<id>: <statement>

  ASSUMPTIONS:
    - @assumption.A<id>: <statement> (confidence: <level>)

  CONSTRAINTS:
    - @constraint.C<id>: <statement>
    - @constraint.C<id>: <statement>

  OPTIONS:
    A. <option A>
    B. <option B>
    C. <option C> (if applicable)

  TRADE-OFFS:
    - @tradeoff.T<id>: <pros/cons summary>

  DECISION:
    <chosen option>

  REASON:
    <why this option beats others>

  RISK:
    <what could go wrong>

  REVERSIBLE:
    true | false

  EVIDENCE:
    - @proof.P<id>
    - @test.X<id>

  FOLLOW-UP:
    - <action>
    - <verification>

Rules:
  [DC-01] Decision canvas MUST be complete before DECISION status = APPROVED.
  [DC-02] Missing FACT or CONSTRAINT blocks approval.
  [DC-03] TRADE-OFF section MUST list at least one pro and one con per option.
  [DC-04] REVERSIBLE flag MUST be set for all decisions.

Navigation:
  Parent: @../INDEX.sdd
  Decisions: @../decisions/INDEX.sdd
  Reasoning: @reasoning-pipeline.sdd

State: +
